From 811c019ee916014b4b651c1d6e052d2cee97ea1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 07:25:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] rw-system.sh: enable MTK ovl bring-up mode when DRM fbdev
 emulation absent

On some MTK devices, hwcomposer.mtk_common.so fails to initialise all
DRM planes with EINVAL on the alpha and pixel blend mode KMS atomic
properties.  The vendor kernel DRM driver does not expose these standard
properties (seen on MT6789/Helio G99, likely other SoCs), causing:

  [DRMDEV] failed to initialize all plane: -19 (ENODEV)
  [DRMDEV] blankDisplay: failed to do atomic commit ret=-22

With no valid plane configuration the display panel never receives a
power-on command and the screen stays black, despite the OS fully
booting and the HWC reporting internal fps activity.

The condition is detectable at runtime: kernels compiled without
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION create /dev/dri/card0 but not /dev/fb0, and
this correlates precisely with the kernels that also lack the atomic
plane properties (both were dropped together in the same MTK kernel
config lineage).

Setting ro.vendor.mtk_ovl_bringup=1 switches the HWC from full-hwc
mode to its bring-up fallback path, bypassing the plane property checks
and allowing the display to come up via GPU composition.

Condition: /dev/dri/card0 present, /dev/fb0 absent,
           /vendor/lib64/hw/hwcomposer.mtk_common.so present.
---
 rw-system.sh | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rw-system.sh b/rw-system.sh
index 7e740ce..239a55a 100644
--- a/rw-system.sh
+++ b/rw-system.sh
@@ -1121,6 +1121,22 @@ if [ "$board" = mt6768 ]; then
 	setprop ro.netflix.bsp_rev MTK6768-19055-1
 fi
 
+# Some MTK devices use hwcomposer.mtk_common.so which requires either
+# working DRM plane properties (alpha, pixel blend mode) or ovl bring-up
+# mode.  When the vendor kernel DRM driver does not expose those standard
+# KMS atomic properties, all plane initialisation fails and the display
+# panel never powers on (black screen).  The reliable runtime signal for
+# this condition is DRM present (/dev/dri/card0) but no fbdev emulation
+# (/dev/fb0 absent) -- the latter is only missing when
+# CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=n, which correlates exactly with the kernels
+# that also lack the atomic plane properties.
+# Setting ro.vendor.mtk_ovl_bringup=1 switches the HWC to its bring-up
+# fallback path, bypassing the plane property checks and allowing display
+# to function via GPU composition.
+if [ -e /dev/dri/card0 ] && [ ! -e /dev/fb0 ] && [ -e /vendor/lib64/hw/hwcomposer.mtk_common.so ]; then
+	resetprop_phh ro.vendor.mtk_ovl_bringup 1
+fi
+
 if [ "$board" = lahaina ]; then
 	setprop ro.netflix.bsp_rev Q875-32774-1
 fi
-- 
